WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:07.490
Speaker 1: OK, one of the things that we have
been kind of discussing, we I mean me with

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:14.589
many in the audience is how we should react
to the deaths of the unvaccinated or more

00:00:14.589 --> 00:00:20.300
specifically, the anti-vaccine individuals,
anti-vaccine individuals who prominently say

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.560
we're against the COVID vaccine.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.610
And then they die of COVID.

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:30.619
I get emails all the time from people saying,
David, you really shouldn't gloat about anti-vaxxers

00:00:30.619 --> 00:00:31.740
dying.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:32.740
And I agree.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.880
I don't gloat about anti-vaxxers dying.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.180
I've said time and again, I feel terribly
about people who have been misled into thinking

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.160
the vaccine is a bad thing.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.520
And then they get COVID and then they die
and their family members grieve, and it's

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.520
sad.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:50.240
I don't gloat about it, but this is super
interesting.

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:58.000
There's a column in the Los Angeles Times
by Michael Hiltzik, which says we should be

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.180
mocking anti-vaxxer deaths, and it is a fascinating
read.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:04.730
We will link to it and I encourage you to
look at it.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:09.910
Michael writes Among all the ways that COVID
affects our lives, the pandemic confronts

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:12.400
us with a profound moral dilemma.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:16.900
How should we react to the deaths of the unvaccinated?

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:22.190
On the one hand, a hallmark of civilized thought
is the sense that every life is precious.

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:26.010
On the other, those who have deliberately
flouted that's not flaunted.

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:31.760
Remember, that's a word flouted sober medical
advice by refusing a vaccine known to reduce

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:36.080
the risk of serious disease from the virus,
including the risk to others and end up in

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:42.140
the hospital or the grave can be viewed as
receiving their just desserts.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:46.950
That's even more true of those who not only
refuse the vaccine for themselves, but publicly

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:49.960
advocated that others do so.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:53.830
It has become common online and in social
media for vaccine refusers and anti-vaccine

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:58.870
advocates to become the target of ridicule
after they come down with COVID and especially

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:00.200
if they die from it.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:04.140
Witness the subreddit Herman Cain Award.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:07.950
The site is named for the former Republican
candidate for president, who became one of

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:13.030
the first political notables to succumb to
the disease after publicly defying social

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:17.400
distancing measures like another site sorry,
anti-vaxxer.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:23.720
The subreddit hosts snippets and photographs
of anti-vaccine advocates often taken at their

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:24.950
death beds.

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:29.280
The issue of how to think about the deaths
of unvaccinated has been thrown into high

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.830
relief locally by the case of Kelly earned
B..

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:35.800
Remember, we covered that that's the Orange
County Republican who was against the mandates

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:38.650
and died of COVID unvaccinated earned.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:43.590
Bee's death promptly came to symbolize the
rift in the social fabric caused by the ravages

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:44.910
of COVID.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:51.780
And then it goes on to say that some of what
is happening with her is bigotry and hate.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.890
Michael Hiltzik has a different take.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:59.180
He says to begin with, let's stipulate not
all unvaccinated people are alike.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:01.540
Some are unvaccinated for legit medical reasons.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:06.540
Children for whom the COVID vaccines haven't
been ruled safe for someone with a real medical

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.490
reason, some may have faced obstacles in getting
to a vaccination site.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:14.620
Others may have been may have refused the
vaccine because they've been deceived by Fox

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:15.800
News or whatever else.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:17.970
The deaths are truly lamentable.

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:22.500
Finally, there are those who have voiced public
opposition to the vaccines.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:24.810
Not all of whom are unvaccinated themselves
earned.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.690
Irn-Bru was in that category.

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:33.330
She asserted opposition not to vaccines but
to mandates, and Hiltzik goes on to say it

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:40.819
should be clear that opposing vaccine mandates
as a as a substitute for opposing vaccination

00:03:40.819 --> 00:03:45.140
itself is a fundamentally incoherent position.

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:50.989
It's little more than the garden variety small-government
Republican ideology.

00:03:50.989 --> 00:03:59.769
Hiltzik points out the significantly lower
vaccination rate of Republicans and says mandates

00:03:59.769 --> 00:04:06.780
do work requirements that people provide evidence
of vaccination have been associated with heightened

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:08.520
vaccine rates.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:13.340
As for whether vaccination mandates are a
slippery slope to more government control,

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:18.989
which many of these people maintain, government
mandates for vaccines have been with us for

00:04:18.989 --> 00:04:24.759
decades and for other kinds wearing seatbelts,
having airbags in cars, banning smoking in

00:04:24.759 --> 00:04:31.270
public places, and that these mandates exist
because the diseases threaten not only the

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:34.720
infected people but also the community.

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:42.839
And Hiltzik goes on to say ultimately that
it is so pernicious that we have these people

00:04:42.839 --> 00:04:49.080
around advocating against vaccines are against
vaccine mandates that in fact, we should be

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:55.030
ridiculing them, that in fact we should be
mocking them and that in the long run, even

00:04:55.030 --> 00:05:02.860
though it feels like a ghoulish thing to do
the same way that vaccine mandates work, mocking

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:12.710
those who are anti-vax, outspokenly anti-vax
or anti mandate and then die actually is effective

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:14.430
at getting people vaccinated.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:18.830
That it might feel wrong, as I have said,
and many of you have said, but that it is

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:24.360
actually a necessary thing to do because of
the public health consequences.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:29.729
Check out Michael Hiltzik opinion piece, and
I would love to hear from you about this.

